Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  17 AUG 94 at 14 20 CLINICAL DATA  32 year old female with a history of an abnormal mammogram with calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL  MASS   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  70    GRADE REMOVED_DATE WITH EXTENSIVE PERINEURAL INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO  CRIBRIFORM  AND SOLID TYPES  30    SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is 1 1cm in maximum diameter and extends to 0 3cm of the inked resection margin  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Microcalcifications are present in association with the invasive carcinoma  Fibrocystic changes are also present  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR  MASS   BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH FLORID EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND DUCTAL PAPILLOMA  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  19 AUG 94 at 18 26                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  Medial  1   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 AUG 94 at 15 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Lesion  1  right breast medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  with localizing wire in place and accompanying mammogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm lesion in greatest diameter directly adjacent to the inked margin  Representative section was frozen as frozen section  1  and kept frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in A through J  The suspicious lesion submitted in D  E  and F  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Inferior right breast tissue   2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue with localizing wire in place and accompanying mammogram  The specimen was inked and sectioned to reveal no suspicious areas  Submitted entirely in K through Q  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST MEDIAL  1   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS INFERIOR  2 LESION   NO SUSPICIOUS AREAS SEEN  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D       