mitted as follows  D  Medial margin  entirely  E  Lateral margin  entirely  F G  Posterior margin  representative  closest  H  Inferior  I  Anterior  J  Superior  K  Tumor  center  R  Additional inferior margin  Labeled  posterior margin right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm yellow tan  irregular  fibrofatty tissue fragment that is inked in black  serially sectioned and entirely submitted as L  Labeled  inferior margin right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm yellow tan  fibrofatty tissue that is marked by a stitch on one side  The stitched surface is inked black  the opposite surface is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as M and N  Also received is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm yellow tan  unmarked soft tissue fragment that is inked in black  bisected  and entirely submitted as O  Labeled  final shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of yellow tan  fibrofatty tissue fragments that are inked in black and entirely submitted as P through Q  Resident  TAN A  INCE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     Frozen section diagnoses  1 and 2 Lymph nodes  right axillary sentinel   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  SOUHAD YOUNES  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  POSTERIOR MARGIN   PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR MARGIN   PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS   PART E  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL  , Suspicious.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 15 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  MUCINOUS  COLLOID  CARCINOMA  INVASIVE  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL ADJACENT TO INVASIVE CARCINOMA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  In the absence of an in situ component  a metastasis cannot be completely excluded  However  the cytomorphology of the tumor is most consistent with a breast primary  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 19 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm piece of firm  fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a white  firm nodule measuring 1 8cm in greatest dimension that focally abuts the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  The specimen is submitted entirely in A through J  with frozen section in J  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , No.
