Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 40 CLINICAL DATA  75 y o  female undergoing excisional biopsy of a left breast mass detected by mammography  Core   adenocarcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITH EXTENSIVE MUCIN PRODUCTION  CELLULAR MUCINOUS CARCINOMA   GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   LATERAL MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of breast tissue with a stitch marking the anterior lateral margin as denoted by the surgeon  The specimen is inked black and the anterior lateral half has been overinked green  It is sectioned to reveal a a firm area 0 3cm in greatest dimension  The firm area is submitted in A  with the remainder submitted in B through I  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  lateral margin tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of breast tissue that is inked and submitted in its entirety in cassette J  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  SMALL FIRM AREA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENT  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION , No.
