 for calponin  SM MHC  and p63 were evaluated  Tumor is noted within lymphatic vessels in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Although much of this intralymphatic tumor has a fragmented and folded appearance suggestive of artifactual displacement  the possibility of focal genuine lymphatic invasion cannot be entirely excluded  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSCTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   RE EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are three containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm axillary tail  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm tan pink skin ellipse with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan pink unremarkable nipple which comes to 0 5cm of the superior skin margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  gray white fibrous scar with an eccentric  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm hemorrhagic focus  The scar abuts the anterior and posterior margins along the inferolateral aspect of the breast  Located 0 3cm lateral to this area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm poorly delineated  firm  nodular  tan pink lesion  which come to 0 2cm of the posterior and 0 1cm of the anterior margins  There are several suspicious tan red nodular areas immediately posterior to the scar  which occupy a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm area and range from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in greatest dimension  The nodules come to 0 2cm of the posterior margin  The nodules are diffuse and are also located in patches throughout the remaining mammary tissue  One of these patches measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and is located in the subareolar anterolateral breast tissue  This area focally abuts the anterior margin  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals several possible tan pink lymph nodes averaging 0 3cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Subareolar anterolateral breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mid lower  central inferior  breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scar  lower outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between scar and nodular area in lower outer breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular area in lower outer breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from axillary tail which may represent lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  axillary contents left   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of tan pink fibrofatty tissue which is sectioned to reveal several tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 6cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three intact lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  final lateral margin left   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of tan pink  fibrofatty tissue with a black stitch along one aspect designating the new margin  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal hemorrhage and dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  Th