cal assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  only is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm excision specimen with localizing wire in place  Inked and stained to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm stellate nodule which abuts the inked resection margin in multiple locations  Submitted entirely in A through E  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
