Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 12 CLINICAL DATA  Left upper outer quadrantectomy of breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  UPPER OUTER  QUADRANTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 3 3    SEE NOTE   2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH EPITHELIOSIS  4  RADIAL SCAR  4  FIBROADENOMA  MICROSCOPIC  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 8cm in greatest dimension  All examined inked surgical margins are negative for carcinoma  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be reported as an addendum  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 37                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a 110 gram resection specimen of breast tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm with contiguous axillary tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm with a long suture designating a breast mass and short suture designating the lower cephalad margin of the axillary tissue  The external surface of the breast tissue and axillary contents is lobulated unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Within the breast tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm mobile well circumbscribed nodule 1 5cm  from the superior aspect and within 0 2cm  of the anterior and deep margins  The external surface is inked black with the posterior aspect inked yellow on black  and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a well circumscribed pink tan mass REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm in greatest dimension extending to within 0 5cm of the anterior resection margin and to within less than 0 1cm of the deep margin  The remaining tissue is strands of white pink rubbery breast parenchyma within lobulated yellow adipose tissue  Within the axilla are multiple large firm lymph nodes which on cross section have a white tan appearance  these range in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The largest three are bisected and submitted in cassettes A and B  Remaining lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassette C  Section code A C Axillary lymph nodes  D Medial en face resection margin  E G Representative sections of the tumor with anterior and deep margins  H K Radial sections through the inferior margin  L N Representative radial sections through the superior margin  O Representative radial section into the axilla  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  UPPER OUTER  QUADRANTECTOMY   report_end  , No.
