fin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Five containers are received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm mastectomy specimen with a overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm  with a suture designating the superior aspect  The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm nipple is unremarkable  The tan skin is unremarkable  The specimen is breadloafed to reveal a nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm in greatest dimension is approximately 2 0cm from the medial margin  1 0cm from the inferior margin  6 0cm from the superior margin and 15 0cm from the lateral margin  Section Code  A  farthest inferiomedial extension of tumor C  section through granular extension of lesion D  section through fibrous region of breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm E  representative deep margin  nearest tumor F  additional section of deep margin  near fibrous area  Labeled  left axilla  low Hot Spot  1  CT 762   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm nodule of fatty tissue  Labeled  left axillary lymph  Level I   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of fatty nodular tissue  H  one lymph node I N  additional lymph nodes  Labeled  left axillary lymph node  Level  2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of fatty fibrous tissue  O  representative lymph node  Level  2 Labeled  left axilla  Hot Spo