e test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 07 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left mastectomy with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm nipple bearing skin ellipse is notable for a 1 0cm superior linear  well healed scar  Within the parenchyma and underlying the scar  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm centrally located firm fibrous area  This is located 2 5cm from the deep margin  6 5cm from the superior margin  6 5cm from the inferior margin  and abuts the skin  There is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined area of fibrous thickening that is located 2 3cm inferior to the first area  It abuts the anterior inferior margin  is 1 5cm from the posterior inferior margin  and is 3 0cm from the inferior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  There is an unattached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular fragment of yellow adipose tissue that is grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A C  Representative sections of larger firm fibrous area  with skin in A  D  Closest posterior margin to larger mass  E F  Second smaller area of firm fibrosis with anterior margin  G  Second smaller area of firm fibrosis with posterior margin  H I  Representative sections of parenchyma away from fibrous areas  with ink representing posterior  J  Representative sections of separate piece of adipose tissue  Within the axillary tail multiple tan white lymph nodes are identified  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension  Whole lymph nodes are submitted in K through M and representative sections of individual lymph nodes are submitted in N  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                 S