ogesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm nodule of breast tissue with a well demarcated  irregular firm and gritty white to gray nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm in size abutting an inked resection margin  A portion of the suspicious nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  submitted entirely in A through I  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , No.
