east carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 59     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THE LYMPH NODES DO NOT CONTAIN KERATIN POSITIVE CARCINOMA CELLS  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 52     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and an accompanying specimen radiograph  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal focally yellow focally white breast parenchyma showing focal cystic changes  No discrete lesions are noted  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes A F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary nodes  is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple firm lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Representative sections of each lymph node are submitted in cassettes G K  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  NO LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_I