Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  23 MAY 94 at 16 00 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA   1 5 CM    SEE NOTE   NOTE  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Tumor comes within 0 2cm of the superior inked resection margin  Frozen section gross impression is confirmed  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  MICROCYTS AND ADENOSIS  AXILLA  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWENTY OF TWENTY LYMPH NODES  2  BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 94 at 15 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of p