haracteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm tan gray rubbery ovoid lymph node with attached adipose tissue  The lymph node is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes A C  The remaining adipose tissue is left in the container  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy  is an oval portion of fibroadipose tissue which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 9cm  The specimen is oriented with two sutures short designates superior margin  long designates lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  There is a linear suture line on the anterior face of the specimen extending from the inferior to the superior margin which measures 4 5cm in length  The sutures are removed and the specimen appears to have been previously partially bisected  Cross sections shows a firm white gray fibrous stellate lesion which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Inside the lesion is a cyst with hemorrhagic material which measures 0 3cm in diameter  This lesion abuts the posterior margin and is located 1 0cm from superior margin  1 7cm from anterior margin and 1 8cm from inferior margin  The remainder of breast tissue has an unremarkable fibrous and fatty parenchyma  Sections of the mass with adjacent margins are submitted in cassettes D G with the nodular lesion submitted in cassette E  Cassettes H and I contain two sec