en receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast carcinoma   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm breast tissue with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is inked superior half in black  the inferior half in blue  and overinked the anterior with green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 2 0cm white firm stellate area located 0 3cm of the anterior  closest resection margin  in the lateral half of the specimen  A biopsy cavity is present in the medial half  Representative sections of the tumor are submitted in A D and the biopsy cavity in E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a fragment of soft tan adipose tissue measuring 6 x 5 x 1cm with an ellipse of skin measuring 2 x  5cm  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in F through I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional interior margin  right breast  are two fragments of adipose tan soft tissue measuring in aggregate 2 x 2 x  5cm  One frag