ned with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy re excision   Received is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm lumpectomy specimen with a small REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm strip of skin  There is a short stitch indicating the superior margin and a long stitch indicating the lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  blue superior margin  red  lateral margin  yellow inferior margin  green medial margin  deep margin black  The specimen is incised to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted in entirety in cassettes A through G  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   Received is a mass of yellow red fatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Dissected are twelve lymph nodes from the axillary pad  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in diameter  The lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes H through J  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   report_end  , No.
