Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 52 CLINICAL DATA  None given                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90   WELL TO MODERATE DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO INKED MARGINS    INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10    MIXED CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID SUBTYPES     ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 8cm in greatest diameter  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Dr Koerner has reviewed this case and agrees with this interpretation  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of p